<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodoric the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">454–526</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodoric the Great was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> who invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at the request of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Emperor Zeno</a>, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> and ruled the peninsula from Ravenna from 493 to 526. He kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>, the senate and the civil administration while his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> formed the army, and built a network of marriage alliances with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> and Thuringians. His mausoleum still stands in Ravenna.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great.jpg" alt="Theodoric the Great" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teodorico_re_dei_Goti_(493-526).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
